License
=======

This repository contains two kinds of material. Each kind keeps its own license.

1. PhET-derived simulation files
--------------------------------

These HTML files are built copies of Faraday's Electromagnetic Lab from
PhET Interactive Simulations, University of Colorado Boulder:

- faradays-electromagnetic-lab_en_adapted-from-phet.html
- faradays-electromagnetic-lab.html
- faradays-electromagnetic-lab_all_adapted-from-phet.html

faradays-electromagnetic-lab.html is a byte-for-byte copy of
faradays-electromagnetic-lab_en_adapted-from-phet.html.

Each file identifies the work as follows:

- Name: Faraday's Electromagnetic Lab
- Project: faradays-electromagnetic-lab
- Version: 1.1.0-dev.0
- Brand: adapted-from-phet
- Copyright 2002-2024, Regents of the University of Colorado
- English build: 2024-10-04 16:13:59 UTC
- All-locales build: 2024-10-02 21:42:08 UTC

The English file and its identical copy have language switching turned off.
The all-locales file starts in English, includes PhET's translations, and
has language switching turned on.

License for these HTML files: CC BY 4.0
----------------------------------------

The notice PhET placed at the top of each file says:

    This file is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0

That is the license for copying and redistributing these HTML files. The
full license is Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

PhET's historical software agreement says the same thing for Regular HTML
Simulation Files released before March 29, 2026. These builds are dated
October 2024.

    https://phet.colorado.edu/en/licensing/html

Required attribution. Keep this sentence readable. PhET allows translation
of it and no other change:

    Simulation by PhET Interactive Simulations, University of Colorado Boulder, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://phet.colorado.edu).

CC BY 4.0 allows use and redistribution, including commercial use, when
that attribution is kept and any changes are indicated. Hosting these files
in a public repository is allowed. See NOTICE.

HTML simulations PhET published after March 29, 2026 are under CC BY-NC 4.0.
That license is not the license of the files in this repository. PhET's
current licensing page describes the newer terms:

    https://phet.colorado.edu/en/licensing
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Source-code license: GNU GPL v3
-------------------------------

PhET licenses the simulation-specific source under the GNU General Public
License v3, and licenses PhET common libraries under the MIT License. The
HTML file header points to the source license as an alternate:

    For alternate source code licensing, see https://github.com/phetsims

The built files embed the source package field "license": "GPL-3.0".
PhET's HTML5 software agreement describes the split: the minified HTML
simulation file is CC BY 4.0, the simulation source is GPLv3, and the
common source is MIT.

    https://phet-dev.colorado.edu/license.html
    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

This repository contains the built HTML files, not the simulation source.
The source repository is:

    https://github.com/phetsims/faradays-electromagnetic-lab

At version 1.1.0-dev.0 that repository's package.json declared
"license": "GPL-3.0", and its LICENSE file was the GPLv3 text. The public
source was removed on 2026-10-09 in commit 63727846a29a0457920efc0433d804890dcf79d1.
The GPLv3 text and package.json remain in git history at commit
8390b87d5585af09f917d18fb7d045c80f0b91db.

Third-party components inside each HTML file keep the licenses printed in
that file's header. Section 2 below does not replace those notices.

Trademarks
----------

The PhET name and PhET logo are trademarks of the Regents of the University
of Colorado. PhET grants permission to use them for attribution. Promotional,
marketing, or advertising use requires a separate license from the University
of Colorado. Contact phethelp@colorado.edu.

adapted-from-phet is PhET's brand for a build that is not an official
simulation published by PhET. The phet and phet-io brands are reserved for
PhET Interactive Simulations.

    https://github.com/phetsims/brand

